cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite it as below, and please state that the
  main theorem is an implication from the printed imports A1-A8 of its section 2.4
  (the moment input U_GJS, Assumption A8(vi), is GJS Theorem 1.1.11 as printed) and
  that the human page readings of audit item C5 are open.
title: >-
  Removal of the spatial cutoff for weakly coupled P(phi)_2: norm convergence of
  the ground-state net on the quasi-local algebra (Part I)
abstract: >-
  Let H(g) be the spatially cutoff P(phi)_2 Hamiltonian, Omega_g its ground state,
  and omega_g the induced state on the time-zero quasi-local algebra. From two printed
  theorems of Glimm, Jaffe and Spencer (Ann. of Math. 100 (1974)), the clustering
  Theorem 1.1.7 and the moment estimate (1.1.16) of Theorem 1.1.11 at B = I, n = 0 and
  any 0 < T < 1, the case they name on p. 629 and specialize to T = 0 in their proof of
  Theorem 1.1.8, together with standard construction inputs,
  the full net (omega_g) converges in norm on every local algebra in the weak-coupling
  region, with an explicit super-polynomial rate; the limit is locally normal,
  translation and Z_2 invariant, and a ground state of the Glimm-Jaffe dynamics in
  the spectral sense. The proof is Hamiltonian, via a local-perturbations-perturb-
  locally estimate built on an exact spectral filter and the exact light cone. The
  repository also contains the working drafts and the adversarial audit trail.
